(ns cohost.http-eve
  "jank-seat hosting for cohost.http (MEMORY-PLAN.md, unit 9), the
   counterpart of cohost/http_eve.clj (JVM) and cohost/http_eve.cljs
   (Node): Eve's own HTTP layer on jank -- eve.http over the host's C
   sockets (one synchronous round trip, as every host's eve.http is) and
   eve.http-server's C++ server -- installed as cohost.http's leaves.

   jank reads this file for cohost.http-eve: it loads a .jank before a
   .cljc and never a .clj, so the JVM and Node seats keep their own files.
   It is loaded only by a run that puts Eve's jank http adapters on the
   module path (eve/adapters/http/jank/src, eve/adapters/http-server/jank/src)
   beside Eve's :jank roots, after eve.host-completion (Eve's namespaces
   load on jank only after it); nothing in cohost.run's AOT graph requires
   it -- the same shape as the other seats' files.

   What the adapter contract's defaults give this seat, unchanged here:
   bodies stay text (the jank adapter has no :byte-streams), and a URL /
   URI stays the layer's tagged map (no :http-value; the shim's toString
   answers its text)."
  (:require [cohost.adapter :as adapter]
            [cohost.http :as http]
            [eve.http :as eve-http]
            [eve.http-server :as eve-http-server]))

(defn install!
  "Install Eve's http leaves over the current host adapter."
  []
  (adapter/install! (assoc (adapter/current)
                           :http-request eve-http/request
                           :http-serve eve-http-server/serve!))
  (http/available?))
